prompts.text:
Now you are ${role_description}

You are in a discussion group, aiming to ${task_description}.

Below is the chat history among you and other teammates.

You are faced with the task:
${task_description}

Below is the chat history among you and other teammates.

You sort a task into one of a fixed list of task families, or say it fits none of them.

# Task
${task}

# Families
${families}

# What to do
Choose the one family whose description fits the task best. If none fits well, choose "new".
Reply with JSON only, one line: {"family": "<a family name from the list, or new>", "why": "<one short sentence>"}

You propose one fix for a stuck step of a team plan. The team is carrying out the task below step by step. One step is stuck, plain code has already tried its own fixes (listed under "Fixes already tried"), and they did not work or were not allowed. Propose exactly ONE edit that lets this step finish. Plain code checks your edit, applies it and re-runs the step; the step counts as fixed only when its checks and its contract pass.

# Task
${task}

# The stuck step (step ${step})
${card}

# Why it is stuck (plain code's diagnosis)
Cause: ${cause}
${evidence}

# The last attempt (trimmed)
${attempt}

# The team
${team}

# Tools and skills available in this run (nothing else exists)
${tools}

# Edits allowed for this cause
${allowed}

# Fixes already tried in this task (never propose one of these again)
${tried}

# Rules
- Exactly one edit, from the allowed list only, in the shape shown for it.
- grant_tool and a new helper's tools may name only tools listed under "Tools and skills available in this run".
- Steps that are done stay as they are; only this step and the steps not yet run may change.
- Do not tell the team to skip checks, citations, sources or the sandbox.

# Reply
Only one JSON object, nothing else:
{"edit": {"op": "<allowed op>", "params": {...}}, "reason": "<why this will let the step finish, at most 300 characters>"}

You are reviewing a teammate's draft for one step of a team plan.

# Task
${task}

${today}

# Your role card
${card}

# The step (step ${number})
${step}

# Inputs the step was given
${inputs}

# The draft, written by ${drafter}
${draft}

# How to review
Judge the draft only against the step's done_when and your own success criteria:
- done_when: ${done_when}
- your success criteria: ${criteria}
If the draft meets them, answer AGREE and write "none" under Issues. Otherwise answer REVISE and list each problem as a numbered issue: what is wrong and how to fix it. Do not rewrite the draft and do not add analysis of your own.

# Format
Your reply MUST use exactly these sections:

## Verdict
AGREE or REVISE

## Issues
1. ...

A helper on a team asked for a ${kind} the team does not have. Choose the one candidate below that can do this job, if any.

Request
- name: ${name}
- kind: ${kind}
- what it does: ${what}
- input: ${input}
- output: ${output}
- for helper: ${helper}
- in step: ${steps}

Candidates
${candidates}

Reply with exactly one candidate id from the list above, or NONE if no candidate can do the job. Write nothing else.

